      "raw_text": "I don't have the newest Annual Report for $SE because its not out yet, but I did set up my Notebooklm awhile.\n\n**Sea Limited** is a leading global consumer internet company headquartered in **Singapore** that was founded in 2009. The company's mission is to better the lives of consumers and small businesses with technology. It is listed on the **New York Stock Exchange** under the symbol \"**SE**\" and operates through three primary business segments: **Shopee** (e-commerce), **SeaMoney/Monee** (digital financial services), and **Garena** (digital entertainment).\n\n### **Core Business Segments**\n*   **Shopee:** This is the largest **e-commerce platform** in Southeast Asia and Taiwan, with a significant and growing presence in **Latin America**, particularly Brazil. Shopee operates a mobile-first, social-focused marketplace model that connects buyers and sellers. In the 2025 fiscal year, Shopee achieved a **Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) of $127.4 billion**, representing a 27% increase year-on-year.\n\n*   **SeaMoney / Monee:** This segment provides a suite of **digital financial services**, including mobile wallet services, payment processing, and consumer and SME credit products like **SPayLater**. It also holds **banking licenses** in Singapore, Indonesia, and the Philippines. By the end of 2025, the credit business reached over **37 million active users** with a total loan principal outstanding of more than **$9 billion**.\n\n*   **Garena:** As a global **game developer and publisher**, Garena provides access to popular mobile and PC online games. Its most successful title is the self-developed battle royale game **Free Fire**, which is available in more than 160 markets. Garena also heavily promotes **esports** to drive user engagement and reported **$2.9 billion in bookings** for 2025.\n\n### **Financial Performance (FY 2025)**\n\n*   **GAAP Revenue:** The company reported total revenue of **$22.9 billion** in 2025, up significantly from $16.8 billion in 2024.\n*   **Profitability:** Sea Limited recorded a **net income of $1.6 billion** and a **total adjusted EBITDA of $3.4 billion** for the full year 2025.\n*   **Cash Position:** As of the end of 2025, the company maintained a strong gross cash position of **$10.5 billion**.\n\n### **Corporate Governance and Leadership**\n\n*   **Founder & CEO:** The company is led by founder **Forrest Xiaodong Li**, who serves as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer.\n*   **Voting Structure:** Sea Limited utilizes a **dual-class voting structure**. As of March 2025, Mr. Li beneficially owned **59.1% of the total voting power** through his sole ownership of all Class B ordinary shares, which carry 15 votes per share.\n*   **Global Workforce:** The company's scale is supported by approximately **80,700 employees** as of late 2024.\n\n### **Geographic Footprint**\n\nSea’s primary operations are concentrated in **Southeast Asia** (including Indonesia, Vietnam, Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia, and Singapore), **Taiwan**, and **Brazil**. Southeast Asia remains its largest revenue contributor, accounting for approximately **70% of total revenue** in 2024.",
      "cleaned_text": "I don't have the newest Annual Report for $SE because its not out yet, but I did set up my Notebooklm awhile. **Sea Limited** is a leading global consumer internet company headquartered in **Singapore** that was founded in 2009. The company's mission is to better the lives of consumers and small businesses with technology. It is listed on the **New York Stock Exchange** under the symbol \"**SE**\" and operates through three primary business segments: **Shopee** (e-commerce), **SeaMoney/Monee** (digital financial services), and **Garena** (digital entertainment). ### **Core Business Segments** * **Shopee:** This is the largest **e-commerce platform** in Southeast Asia and Taiwan, with a significant and growing presence in **Latin America**, particularly Brazil. Shopee operates a mobile-first, social-focused marketplace model that connects buyers and sellers. In the 2025 fiscal year, Shopee achieved a **Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) of $127.4 billion**, representing a 27% increase year-on-year. * **SeaMoney / Monee:** This segment provides a suite of **digital financial services**, including mobile wallet services, payment processing, and consumer and SME credit products like **SPayLater**. It also holds **banking licenses** in Singapore, Indonesia, and the Philippines. By the end of 2025, the credit business reached over **37 million active users** with a total loan principal outstanding of more than **$9 billion**. * **Garena:** As a global **game developer and publisher**, Garena provides access to popular mobile and PC online games. Its most successful title is the self-developed battle royale game **Free Fire**, which is available in more than 160 markets. Garena also heavily promotes **esports** to drive user engagement and reported **$2.9 billion in bookings** for 2025. ### **Financial Performance (FY 2025)** * **GAAP Revenue:** The company reported total revenue of **$22.9 billion** in 2025, up significantly from $16.8 billion in 2024. * **Profitability:** Sea Limited recorded a **net income of $1.6 billion** and a **total adjusted EBITDA of $3.4 billion** for the full year 2025. * **Cash Position:** As of the end of 2025, the company maintained a strong gross cash position of **$10.5 billion**. ### **Corporate Governance and Leadership** * **Founder & CEO:** The company is led by founder **Forrest Xiaodong Li**, who serves as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer. * **Voting Structure:** Sea Limited utilizes a **dual-class voting structure**. As of March 2025, Mr. Li beneficially owned **59.1% of the total voting power** through his sole ownership of all Class B ordinary shares, which carry 15 votes per share. * **Global Workforce:** The company's scale is supported by approximately **80,700 employees** as of late 2024. ### **Geographic Footprint** Sea’s primary operations are concentrated in **Southeast Asia** (including Indonesia, Vietnam, Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia, and Singapore), **Taiwan**, and **Brazil**. Southeast Asia remains its largest revenue contributor, accounting for approximately **70% of total revenue** in 2024.",
      "english_translation": "I don't have the newest Annual Report for $SE because its not out yet, but I did set up my Notebooklm awhile. **Sea Limited** is a leading global consumer internet company headquartered in **Singapore** that was founded in 2009. The company's mission is to better the lives of consumers and small businesses with technology. It is listed on the **New York Stock Exchange** under the symbol \"**SE**\" and operates through three primary business segments: **Shopee** (e-commerce), **SeaMoney/Monee** (digital financial services), and **Garena** (digital entertainment). ### **Core Business Segments** * **Shopee:** This is the largest **e-commerce platform** in Southeast Asia and Taiwan, with a significant and growing presence in **Latin America**, particularly Brazil. Shopee operates a mobile-first, social-focused marketplace model that connects buyers and sellers. In the 2025 fiscal year, Shopee achieved a **Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) of $127.4 billion**, representing a 27% increase year-on-year. * **SeaMoney / Monee:** This segment provides a suite of **digital financial services**, including mobile wallet services, payment processing, and consumer and SME credit products like **SPayLater**. It also holds **banking licenses** in Singapore, Indonesia, and the Philippines. By the end of 2025, the credit business reached over **37 million active users** with a total loan principal outstanding of more than **$9 billion**. * **Garena:** As a global **game developer and publisher**, Garena provides access to popular mobile and PC online games. Its most successful title is the self-developed battle royale game **Free Fire**, which is available in more than 160 markets. Garena also heavily promotes **esports** to drive user engagement and reported **$2.9 billion in bookings** for 2025. ### **Financial Performance (FY 2025)** * **GAAP Revenue:** The company reported total revenue of **$22.9 billion** in 2025, up significantly from $16.8 billion in 2024. * **Profitability:** Sea Limited recorded a **net income of $1.6 billion** and a **total adjusted EBITDA of $3.4 billion** for the full year 2025. * **Cash Position:** As of the end of 2025, the company maintained a strong gross cash position of **$10.5 billion**. ### **Corporate Governance and Leadership** * **Founder & CEO:** The company is led by founder **Forrest Xiaodong Li**, who serves as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer. * **Voting Structure:** Sea Limited utilizes a **dual-class voting structure**. As of March 2025, Mr. Li beneficially owned **59.1% of the total voting power** through his sole ownership of all Class B ordinary shares, which carry 15 votes per share. * **Global Workforce:** The company's scale is supported by approximately **80,700 employees** as of late 2024. ### **Geographic Footprint** Sea’s primary operations are concentrated in **Southeast Asia** (including Indonesia, Vietnam, Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia, and Singapore), **Taiwan**, and **Brazil**. Southeast Asia remains its largest revenue contributor, accounting for approximately **70% of total revenue** in 2024.",
